{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Having Second Thoughts"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Having Second Thoughts"}, {"type": "position", "content": 3}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 11}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.1"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe hypothetical situations in written and spoken interactions according to work and social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn9le11ob03re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The Third Conditional - Talking Hypothetically About the Past"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "The third conditional is used to talk about the past in a hypothetical way. That is, to refer to things that did not happen in the past, but to imagine what might have happened if they had. You can use the third conditional to talk about regrets (things that you wish had been different, or things that you wish you had done). "}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can use the structures <span class=\"italic\">would have</span>, <span class=\"italic\">should have</span> and <span class=\"italic\">could have</span> with the third conditional to be precise about meaning.<br/><br/>   <span class=\"underline\"><span class=\"italic\">Could have</span></span> (+ past participle) means that something was possible in the past, or you had the ability to do something in the past, but that you didn't do it.<br/> You also use<span class=\"underline\"><span class=\"italic\"> could have</span></span> to make a guess about something that happened in the past. <br/>Example:<span class=\"italic\"> How <span class=\"strong\">could </span> my life <span class=\"strong\">have unfolded</span> if I hadn't gone to Paris where I met a famous photographer?"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"underline\"><span class=\"italic\">Should have</span></span> (+ past participle) means something would have been a good idea, but you didn't do it. You can use it to give advice about the past when you say it to someone else, or to express regret about what you did or didn't do when you're talking about yourself.<br/> Example: <span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">should have told</span> him how I felt. </span> (I regret not telling him how I felt)."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Use <span class=\"underline\"><span class=\"italic\">would have</span></span> ( + past participle) to talk about something you wanted to do but didn't, or a hypothetical situation in the past.<br/>Example:<span class=\"italic\"> If you hadn't taken an opportunity that you took, you <span class=\"strong\">would have been</span> regretful. </span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Remember the structure of the third conditional: <br> If + subject + had + past participle, subject + could/would/should have + past participle"}, {"type": "example", "content": "What if her parents hadn't pushed her into that profession?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "If she had had the courage to defy her parents and travel, she could have discovered a new passion. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "How could my life have unfolded if I hadn't gone to Paris where I met a famous photographer who unexpectedly snapped a picture of me and changed my career path from teaching to modelling?\u201d"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Many people wonder how their lives would have turned out if things had been different."}, {"type": "example", "content": " Would she have traveled the world and become a journalist?"}, {"type": "example", "content": " If I hadn't started this blog, I wouldn't have connected with so many wonderful people. If I hadn't won the lottery I couldn't have traveled to Europe and changed my outlook on life."}, {"type": "example", "content": " If you hadn't taken an opportunity that you took, you would have been regretful."}, {"type": "example", "content": " I should have told him how I felt."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Talking about Wishes"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "When you want to talk about  imaginary situations in the past, you can use <span class=\"italic\">wish</span> plus the past participle of the verb. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you talk about wishes, you talk about things you wanted that were probably not possible, or for some reason impossible.<br/><br/>  You use <span class=\"underline\"><span class=\"italic\">wish</span> + had + past participle</span>  to talk about wishes in the past.<br/><br/>  For example:<br/>  <span class=\"italic\">Sometimes I <span class=\"strong\">wish I had tried</span> skydiving.</span><br/>  (I didn't try skydiving.)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "You would say I wish I had kissed that boy, or, I wish I had tried skydiving, I could tell you what it was like to fly."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I wish I hadn't been afraid, I would have succeeded!"}, {"type": "example", "content": " I wish I had used my time more wisely. "}, {"type": "example", "content": " I wish I had gone on that trip."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "unexpectedly"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "used to describe an action  that is surprising because you were not expecting it"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adverb) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I met a famous photographer who unexpectedly snapped a picture of me. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le11ob03aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about choices."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to snap a picture"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "take a picture"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: That  photographer  who unexpectedly snapped.a picture of me, changed my life."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le11ob03aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to push someone into"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " to persuade or encourage someone to do something that they may not want to do"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: If her parents hadn't pushed her into Medicine, she would have been a journalist."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le11ob03aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to defy"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to \u200brefuse to \u200bobey a \u200bperson, \u200bdecision, \u200blaw, \u200bsituation, etc "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  If she had had the courage to defy her parents and travel, she could have discovered a new passion."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le11ob03aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "alternate"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "if something happens on alternate days, weeks etc, it happens on one day and not the next, and continues in this pattern"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We  might have had an alternate reality."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le11ob03aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "regret"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "sadness that you feel about something, especially because you wish it had not happened"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We might have some regrets."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le11ob03aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "regretful"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "someone who is regretful feels sorry or disappointed"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: If you hadn't taken an opportunity that you took, you would have been regretful."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le11ob03aud07"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "skydiving"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the sport of jumping from a plane and falling through the sky before opening a parachute\t "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I wish I had tried skydiving. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le11ob03aud08"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "wisely"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "having the power of discerning and judging properly as to what is true or right "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adverb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I wish I had used my time more wisely."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le11ob03aud09"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Talk about the things you wish for in the future and the things you wished for in the past. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Ask a partner to share his/her wishes for the past and the future."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write a dialogue in which you and your partner discuss your wishes for the future."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Read the dialogue aloud with your partner."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I talk about wishes in the present and past."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I ask about my partner's wishes in the present and the past."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write about wishes in the present and the past."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I read the dialogue with a partner about wishes."}]}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [0], "type": "WLC", "questions": [], "img_path": "", "id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about emotions, opinions, behavior and work."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "  I can talk about hypothetical situations in the past. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about what I wish for in the past, present or future."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " How would your life have been different if you'd chosen to go to a different school?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " If you hadn't lived in your current house, where would you have lived?"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}]}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attempt left"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct", "allo